\
1969 Lamborghini Miura SV v1.0b3 (0.5) (beta 3).  Raw specs, top speed, acceleration, and all coordinates (license plates, exhausts, wheels, lights) are done, interior and model and skins done, engine sounds not done, and, most importantly, handling not done.  I've tried my best but I'm not a Miura expert and feedback is very much appreciated since I'm not too sure how a Miura should handle.\
\
The models are about 1400 and 700 polys, body, and interior, respectively.  The wheels are about 300, plus transparancies on the hub and brake disc.  I also smoothed the wheel fenders on the body a bit and re-skinned the badges.\
\
Aside from final tweakings and handling, the only thing left really is engine-sound scouting.\
\
Primary feedback should be sent as a PM to me in Ambrosia Forums (username is Buzzzzy, with four Z's), or a post in the Miura developement topic in Ambrosia Forums, and if you don't have an account, use my e-mail as a last resort (I hardly ever check it).  E-mail is: buzzworld_buzzyeah@yahoo.com.\
\
You can use this plug-in however you like, put parts in your plug-ins, modify it, pimp it, tweak it, take credit for it, re-release it, sell it, whatever, credit is appreciated but not demanded.  Re-release without permission or take credit for it at your own risk, I have every right to ask the moderators of the area where it is re-released to take it down (I already have once).  As long as you give credit, and permission is appreciated, it should be perfectly fine (I'm rather loose about it, as long as you notify me or at least give substantial credit I'm usually fine with it).\
